---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Federal series profiles
crumbs: [[null, "Federal series"]]
---
{% import "macros.njk" as m %}
<h1>Federal series profiles</h1>
<p class="emst-lede">For federal HR specialists, classifiers and training officers: each OPM occupational series with the EMST role variants crosswalked to it, the major duties and competencies of those variants, and the series' current status.</p>
{{ m.hrDisclaimer() }}
<p>Series status comes from the EMST OPM series register. Where OPM has proposed realigning a series, the profile says <strong>proposed, not final</strong> and keeps the current series code until OPM decides. Only established core competencies appear in these HR views; module editorial sections and emerging content are left out and counted.</p>
{{ m.statFigure(emst.series.length, "Series in the register", emst.figures.series) }}
<div class="emst-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="OPM series">
<table class="usa-table usa-table--compact usa-table--striped">
  <caption>OPM occupational series in the EMST register</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Series</th><th scope="col">Title</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col" class="emst-num">Draft role crosswalk rows</th><th scope="col" class="emst-num">Federal variants in this build</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in emst.series %}
  <tr><td><a href="{{ s.url | url }}">{{ s.code }}</a></td><td>{{ s.title }}</td><td>{{ "Realignment proposed, not final" if s.realignment else (s.seriesStatus | titlecase) }}</td><td class="emst-num">{{ s.roleRows.length }}</td><td class="emst-num">{{ s.fedVariants.length }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
